    "content": "The Masters course record is a 9-under-par 63, achieved by Nick Price in 1986 and matched by Greg Norman in 1996, both at Augusta National Golf Club. This record has stood for 40 years, with numerous players coming close, but none breaking 63 in tournament history.Key Course Records18-Hole Record (63): Nick Price (1986, third round) and Greg Norman (1996, first round).72-Hole Record (268): Dustin Johnson in 2020 (-20).Amateur 18-Hole Record (66): Ken Venturi in 1956.Lowest 18-Hole Score (Non-Tournament): Reported to be 61 by Jeff Knox.Notable Near MissesSeveral players have recorded 8-under 64, including Jordan Spieth and Rory McIlroy.Gary Player holds the record for most consecutive cuts made, with 23.Tiger Woods has a best round of 65 at the Masters.Despite modern advancements in equipment and player power, the record set by Price with a wooden driver in 1986 remains one of the longest-standing, lowest scores in major championship history.",
